          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "meditor, meditārī — \"to think over; to rehearse, to practise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ōrātiōnem tōtam noctem meditābātur. He rehearsed his speech all night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: meditor, meditārī, meditātus sum. To think over, and to practise, like a speaker rehearsing. English meditate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "meditor is usually traced to the same root as medeor \"to heal\" (Lewis & Short compare medeor and remedium), a root meaning \"to take fitting measures\". English meditate comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
